---
description: Scope format and typecheck while iterating; full suite only at the end
alwaysApply: true
---

After modifying code files, format only those files and typecheck only the
projects they belong to:

```bash
pnpm exec prettier --write --cache <changed-files>
pnpm typecheck:changed
```

Do not run `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm format:check`, or `pnpm check`
after every edit. Full-repo checks fan out across the monorepo and can exhaust
RAM or thrash the disk.

Before marking work complete, run the orchestrated suite once from the repo root:

```bash
pnpm check
```

`pnpm check` already includes lint, format:check, typecheck, and test:changed.
Do not run those scripts individually and then also run `pnpm check`.

Use `pnpm format` only when you need to auto-fix Prettier across the repo.
Use `pnpm test:changed` for fast test iteration when you changed behavior
covered by tests.
